{"abstract":[{"text":"Acquires ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"context"},{"type":"text","text":" and sets it as the thread-default context for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"current thread. This will cause certain asynchronous operations","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(such as most "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"..\/gio\/index.html","isActive":true},{"text":"-based I\/O) which are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"started in this thread to run under ","type":"text"},{"code":"context","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and deliver their"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"results to its main loop, rather than running under the global"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"default main context in the main thread. Note that calling this function","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"changes the context returned by [func"},{"code":"GLib.MainContext.get_thread_default","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"],","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not the one returned by [func","type":"text"},{"code":"GLib.MainContext.default","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"], so it does not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"affect the context used by functions like [func"},{"code":"GLib.idle_add","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"]."}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/MainContextRef\/pushThreadDefault()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/glib\/maincontextref\/pushthreaddefault()"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/MainContextRef","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/MainContextRef\/MainContextProtocol-Implementations"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"pushThreadDefault"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Normally you would call this function shortly after creating a new"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"thread, passing it a [struct"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/MainContext","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"] which will be run by a"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"[struct"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/MainLoop"},{"type":"text","text":"] in that thread, to set a new default context for all"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"async operations in that thread. In this case you may not need to"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"ever call [method"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GLib.MainContext.pop_thread_default"},{"type":"text","text":"], assuming you want"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the new [struct"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/MainContext","isActive":true},{"text":"] to be the default for the whole lifecycle","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"of the thread.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you don’t have control over how the new thread was created (e.g."},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in the new thread isn’t newly created, or if the thread life","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"cycle is managed by a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/ThreadPool","type":"reference"},{"text":"), it is always suggested to wrap","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"the logic that needs to use the new [struct"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/MainContext","isActive":true},{"text":"] inside a","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"[method"},{"code":"GLib.MainContext.push_thread_default","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"] \/","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"[method"},{"code":"GLib.MainContext.pop_thread_default","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"] pair, otherwise threads that","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"are re-used will end up never explicitly releasing the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"[struct"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/MainContext","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"] reference they hold.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In some cases you may want to schedule a single operation in a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"non-default context, or temporarily use a non-default context in","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the main thread. In that case, you can wrap the call to the"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"asynchronous operation inside a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"[method"},{"code":"GLib.MainContext.push_thread_default","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"] \/"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"[method"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GLib.MainContext.pop_thread_default"},{"type":"text","text":"] pair, but it is up to you to"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ensure that no other asynchronous operations accidentally get","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"started while the non-default context is active."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Beware that libraries that predate this function may not correctly"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"handle being used from a thread with a thread-default context. For example,","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"see "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"g_file_supports_thread_contexts()"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"extendedModule":"GLib","modules":[{"name":"GLib"}],"externalID":"s:4GLib19MainContextProtocolPAAE17pushThreadDefaultyyF::SYNTHESIZED::s:4GLib14MainContextRefV","title":"pushThreadDefault()","symbolKind":"method","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"pushThreadDefault"},{"text":"()","kind":"text"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Method","role":"symbol"},"references":{"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib/ThreadPool":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"ThreadPool","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GThreadPool"},{"type":"text","text":" struct represents a thread pool."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/ThreadPool","url":"\/documentation\/glib\/threadpool","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ThreadPool"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ThreadPool","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib","title":"GLib","abstract":[],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/glib","kind":"symbol","role":"collection"},"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib/MainContextRef":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MainContextRef","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/glib\/maincontextref","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/MainContextRef","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GMainContext"},{"type":"text","text":" struct is an opaque data"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"type representing a set of sources to be handled in a main loop."}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MainContextRef"}],"title":"MainContextRef"},"../gio/index.html":{"identifier":"..\/gio\/index.html","title":"Gio","titleInlineContent":[{"text":"Gio","type":"text"}],"type":"link","url":"..\/gio\/index.html"},"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib/MainContextRef/MainContextProtocol-Implementations":{"type":"topic","abstract":[],"role":"collectionGroup","url":"\/documentation\/glib\/maincontextref\/maincontextprotocol-implementations","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/MainContextRef\/MainContextProtocol-Implementations","title":"MainContextProtocol Implementations","kind":"article"},"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib/MainContext":{"title":"MainContext","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/MainContext","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MainContext"}],"url":"\/documentation\/glib\/maincontext","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MainContext"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"code":"GMainContext","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" struct is an opaque data","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"type representing a set of sources to be handled in a main loop."}]},"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib/MainContextRef/pushThreadDefault()":{"url":"\/documentation\/glib\/maincontextref\/pushthreaddefault()","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Acquires "},{"code":"context","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and sets it as the thread-default context for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"current thread. This will cause certain asynchronous operations"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(such as most ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"..\/gio\/index.html","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"-based I\/O) which are","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"started in this thread to run under "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"context"},{"type":"text","text":" and deliver their"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"results to its main loop, rather than running under the global"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"default main context in the main thread. Note that calling this function","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"changes the context returned by [func","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GLib.MainContext.get_thread_default"},{"type":"text","text":"],"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not the one returned by [func"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GLib.MainContext.default"},{"type":"text","text":"], so it does not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"affect the context used by functions like [func","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GLib.idle_add"},{"text":"].","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/MainContextRef\/pushThreadDefault()","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"pushThreadDefault","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"pushThreadDefault()","type":"topic"},"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib/MainLoop":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/MainLoop","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"MainLoop","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","title":"MainLoop","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MainLoop"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GMainLoop"},{"text":" struct is an opaque data type","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"representing the main event loop of a GLib or GTK application."}],"url":"\/documentation\/glib\/mainloop"}}}